,{"name":"Kim Carr","party":"Labor","person_id":"tvfy_10103","person_slug":"kim-carr","vote":"no"},{"name":"Louise Pratt","party":"Labor","person_id":"tvfy_10714","person_slug":"louise-pratt","vote":"no"},{"name":"Mark Bishop","party":"Labor","person_id":"tvfy_10048","person_slug":"mark-bishop","vote":"no"},{"name":"Mark Furner","party":"Labor","person_id":"tvfy_10710","person_slug":"mark-furner","vote":"no"},{"name":"Mathias Cormann","party":"Liberal","person_id":"tvfy_10148","person_slug":"mathias-cormann","vote":"no"},{"name":"Michael Forshaw","party":"Labor","person_id":"tvfy_10235","person_slug":"michael-forshaw","vote":"no"},{"name":"Michaelia Cash","party":"Liberal","person_id":"tvfy_10707","person_slug":"michaelia-cash","vote":"no"},{"name":"Mitch Fifield","party":"Liberal","person_id":"tvfy_10224","person_slug":"mitch-fifield","vote":"no"},{"name":"Nick Xenophon","party":"Centre Alliance","person_id":"tvfy_10717","person_slug":"nick-xenophon","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Nigel Scullion","party":"Country Liberal Party","person_id":"tvfy_10569","person_slug":"nigel-scullion","vote":"no"},{"name":"Rachel Siewert","party":"Greens","person_id":"tvfy_10584","person_slug":"rachel-siewert","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Richard Colbeck","party":"Liberal","person_id":"tvfy_10131","person_slug":"richard-colbeck","vote":"no"},{"name":"Ron Boswell","party":"Nationals","person_id":"tvfy_10057","person_slug":"ron-boswell","vote":"no"},{"name":"Russell Trood","party":"Liberal","person_id":"tvfy_10640","person_slug":"russell-trood","vote":"no"},{"name":"Sarah Hanson-Young","party":"Greens","person_id":"tvfy_10711","person_slug":"sarah-hanson-young","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Scott Ludlam","party":"Greens","person_id":"tvfy_10713","person_slug":"scott-ludlam","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Scott Ryan","party":"PRES","person_id":"tvfy_10715","person_slug":"scott-ryan","vote":"no"},{"name":"Stephen Parry","party":"PRES","person_id":"tvfy_10507","person_slug":"stephen-parry","vote":"no"},{"name":"Steve Fielding","party":"Family First","person_id":"tvfy_10221","person_slug":"steve-fielding","vote":"no"},{"name":"Steve Hutchins","party":"Labor","person_id":"tvfy_10323","person_slug":"steve-hutchins","vote":"no"},{"name":"Sue Boyce","party":"Liberal","person_id":"tvfy_10062","person_slug":"sue-boyce","vote":"no"},{"name":"Trish Crossin","party":"Labor","person_id":"tvfy_10161","person_slug":"trish-crossin","vote":"no"},{"name":"Ursula Stephens","party":"Labor","person_id":"tvfy_10609","person_slug":"ursula-stephens","vote":"no"}],"name":"Motions - Legislative Power of the Territories - Against federal interference","noes":49,"question":"The majority voted against a [motion](http://www.openaustralia.org/senate/?id=2009-11-26.47.2) introduced by Greens Senator [Sarah Hanson-Young](http://publicwhip-rails.openaustraliafoundation.org.au/mp.php?mpn=Sarah_Hanson-Young&mpc=Senate&house=senate) also on behalf of Liberal Senator [Gary Humphries](http://publicwhip-rails.openaustraliafoundation.org.au/mp.php?mpn=Gary_Humphries&mpc=Senate&house=senate). The motion was: _That the Senate recognises the [sovereignty](http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sovereignty) of the territory parliaments to legislate within the powers conferred on them by the [Federal Parliament](http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Federal_Parliament), without interference from the Federal Government._ In supporting this motion and crossing the floor to vote in favour of it, Senator Humphries rebelled against his party.(Read more about what it means to rebel in our [FAQ Section](http://publicwhip-rails.openaustraliafoundation.org.au/faq.php#rebelandfree). ) Relevantly, he is one of the two senators representing the [Australian Capital Territory](http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Australian_Capital_Territory). _Background to the motion_ Three Australian territories have some level of self-government: the [Australian Capital Territory](http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Australian_Capital_Territory) (ACT), [Northern Territory](http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Northern_Territory) and [Norfolk Island](http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Norfolk_Island). However, the federal government still has full power to legislate over them and can override laws made by territory parliaments.(Read more about Australian territories on Wikipedia [here](http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Australian_territories#Background_and_overview). ) This occurred in respect of same sex marriage legislation passed in the ACT before being disallowed by the federal government.(Read more about this [here](http://publicwhip-rails.openaustraliafoundation.org.au/division.php?date=2006-06-15&number=1&dmp=1&house=senate).","result":"negative","slug":"division-federal-senate-1776","source_url":"https://theyvoteforyou.org.au/divisions/senate/2009-11-26/5"}
